BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Stanford Center for Continuing Medical Education] ENT Expert Up C
 lose: Latest Advances in Rhinoplasty and Sinus Surgery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T130000
DTSTAMP:20260811T142013Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-52876449028518-52876449029543@local-events
DESCRIPTION:OverviewThis session will explore advanced surgical techniques
  and decision-making strategies in rhinoplasty that address both aesthetic
  goals and functional nasal airflow\, while also examining the complexitie
 s of different types of sinusitis and the role of surgery as a definitive 
 treatment option within appropriate patient care pathways. The activity wi
 ll highlight how structural and preservation approaches can be tailored to
  optimize form and function\, including in complex and revision cases\,\n\
 nAges: All ages\nSource: https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverv
 iew?P=5&EID=56919\nLast synced: 2026-08-11 07:20 PDT
URL:https://stanford.cloud-cme.com/course/courseoverview?P=5&EID=56919
END:VEVENT
